{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 1, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 6076572351235212902, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "answered sort_a; measured {'sort_a': 0.18694166900240816, 'sort_b': 0.43954832799499854}\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"README.md": {"bytes": 88, "mtime": 1792286047.5181382, "sha256": "6e8586b6ca7cfdf9188464efa2de5c045956454e61daeae1790e4f109a0982cb"}, "RESULT.md": {"bytes": 15, "mtime": 1792469281.8523736, "sha256": "0f6b2f146d8cf7e3033b9f4de591f774390b66c828e8f0330f4034378211bb29"}, "bench/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1792286047.5181382, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "bench/sorts.py": {"bytes": 679, "mtime": 1792286047.5181382, "sha256": "7d6155a3280716667ff617d8625f9364eab6a92027fa7c1a42052397ebc54355"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/bd7d395222b128ce383be942329867251f75b5f0/omp", "-p", "Which of `sort_a` and `sort_b` in `bench/sorts.py` is faster on 100k random ints? Write the answer to `RESULT.md` as a line `faster: <name>`.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/step7-opus-1019-S7C/omp-32/transcripts/without/trig-omp-experiment/9/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/step7-opus-1019-S7C/omp-32/cells/without/trig-omp-experiment/9/workspace", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "with", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/16.4.8 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/bd7d395222b128ce383be942329867251f75b5f0/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Measuring rather than guessing \u2014 insort is O(n\u00b2) but its moves run in C, so the result isn't obvious.\n`sort_a` is faster. On 100k random ints it took about 0.17s, and `sort_b` took about 0.43s, so `sort_a` is roughly 2.5\u00d7 faster. Each time is the best of 3 runs on the same seeded input, and both outputs matched `sorted(xs)`.\n\nThe reason is that `sort_a` is a merge sort, which scales as O(n log n). `sort_b` inserts each value into a sorted list with `bisect.insort`, which scales as O(n\u00b2). That shifting is done in fast C code, which keeps `sort_b` close at this size, but the gap will grow with larger inputs.\n\nI wrote `faster: sort_a` to `RESULT.md`.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 4, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 36802, "requests_cache_write": 111081, "requests_cost_usd": 0.5799254, "requests_count": 4, "requests_input_uncached": 10, "requests_output": 856, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-experiment:claude-opus-5-5:trial9", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 197, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T04:07:45.846285+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 19.236, "t_checker_s": 0.825, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-experiment", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens":